To incorporate the `RMD` (Remove Directory) and `NOOP` (No Operation) commands into the sequence of client requests, we will need to determine logical placements for these commands. Here’s a modified version of the original sequence, including `RMD` and `NOOP`:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
NOOP
LIST
RMD directory_name
QUIT
```

In this modified sequence:
- The `NOOP` command has been added after the `PORT` command, which is a common place to include it to keep the connection alive.
- The `RMD` command is added before the `QUIT` command, assuming you want to remove a directory before closing the session. You would replace `directory_name` with the actual name of the directory you want to remove. 

Make sure to adjust the position of the `RMD` command according to your specific needs in the context of the session

